@ApiFeatures_HostAddress = http://localhost:5091
@ApiFeatures_HttpsAddress = https://localhost:7123

#if (EnableOpenAPI)
### OpenAPI document (v3.2 with QUERY support)
GET {{ApiFeatures_HostAddress}}/openapi/v1.json
Accept: application/json

###
#endif

### Weather forecast
GET {{ApiFeatures_HostAddress}}/weatherforecast/
Accept: application/json

###

### HTTP QUERY method - search with a request body
QUERY {{ApiFeatures_HostAddress}}/search
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "key",
  "categories": ["Electronics"],
  "maxPrice": 200
}

###

### HTTP QUERY method - all electronics
QUERY {{ApiFeatures_HostAddress}}/search
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "categories": ["Electronics"]
}

###

### Large payload (test response compression with Accept-Encoding: zstd)
GET {{ApiFeatures_HostAddress}}/large-payload
Accept: application/json
Accept-Encoding: zstd, br, gzip

###

### Large payload (gzip only for comparison)
GET {{ApiFeatures_HostAddress}}/large-payload
Accept: application/json
Accept-Encoding: gzip

###

# =====================================================================
# C# unions
# =====================================================================

### Unions: return type — Dog case (STJ serializes the active case)
GET {{ApiFeatures_HostAddress}}/pets/0
Accept: application/json

###

### Unions: return type — Cat case
GET {{ApiFeatures_HostAddress}}/pets/1
Accept: application/json

###

### Unions: OpenAPI describes the union return with anyOf: [Dog, Cat]
# Look at components.schemas.Pet in the response.
GET {{ApiFeatures_HostAddress}}/openapi/v1.json
Accept: application/json

###

### Unions: body param — reference an existing pet (string case)
POST {{ApiFeatures_HostAddress}}/pets/adopt
Content-Type: application/json

"Rex"

###

### Unions: body param — register a new pet (Dog object case)
POST {{ApiFeatures_HostAddress}}/pets/adopt
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Fido" }

###

# =====================================================================
# async validation
# =====================================================================

### Async validation: a registered email is rejected by the async [UniqueEmail] rule
POST {{ApiFeatures_HostAddress}}/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "admin@example.com", "displayName": "Admin" }

###

### Async validation: a new email is accepted
POST {{ApiFeatures_HostAddress}}/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "brand-new@example.com", "displayName": "Newbie" }

###

### Async validation: a weekend date is rejected by async IAsyncValidatableObject
POST {{ApiFeatures_HostAddress}}/reservations
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "guest@example.com", "date": "2026-07-25" }

###

### Async validation: a weekday is accepted
POST {{ApiFeatures_HostAddress}}/reservations
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "guest@example.com", "date": "2026-07-22" }

###

# =====================================================================
# TLS channel binding token access (.NET 11 Preview 7, #67436)
# =====================================================================

### Channel binding over HTTPS — returns the tls-server-end-point token info
# Run with the 'https' profile: dotnet run --project ApiFeatures --launch-profile https
GET {{ApiFeatures_HttpsAddress}}/channel-binding
Accept: application/json

###

### Channel binding over plain HTTP — HttpsRedirection sends a 307 to the HTTPS URL
# (the endpoint's no-TLS branch only runs if HTTPS redirection is bypassed)
GET {{ApiFeatures_HostAddress}}/channel-binding
Accept: application/json

###

